{"v": 1, "key": "cu-cu24", "cards": [{"id": "u2.t.fossil", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">FOS<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">sil<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"fossil\" data-audio=\"audio/fossil.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: fossil\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"fossil\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"60\" rx=\"70\" ry=\"40\" class=\"f7\"/><path d=\"M50 60 Q100 20 150 60 Q100 100 50 60\" class=\"f2\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"60\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"75\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"75\" y2=\"70\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"48\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"72\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"105\" y1=\"48\" x2=\"105\" y2=\"72\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"70\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">bones in rock<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">The preserved remains or traces of an organism that lived long ago.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>化石<\/b>：很久以前生活过的生物的遗体或遗迹被保存下来。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">fossil comes from Latin fossilis = dug up.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">fossil 来自拉丁语：被挖出来的东西。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What is a fossil?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">The preserved remains or traces of an ancient organism.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.transitional-fossil", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">tran<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">SI<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tion<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">al<\/span> <span class=\"st\">FOS<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">sil<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"transitional fossil\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: transitional fossil\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"transitional fossil\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"52.3\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Fish<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"63.5\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">with<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"74.7\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">fins<\/text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"73.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"73.0,60.0 68.5,62.2 68.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"44.4\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Tiktaalik<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"53.6\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">(fins +<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"62.8\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">neck +<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">wrist<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"81.2\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">bones)<\/text><line x1=\"127.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"141.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"141.0,60.0 136.5,62.2 136.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"58.275\" font-size=\"7.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Four-legged<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"66.975\" font-size=\"7.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">animal<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A fossil that shows traits of both an older group and the group that came after it.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>过渡化石<\/b>：同时具有较早类群和后来类群特征的化石。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">transition = going across. A bridge fossil.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">transition = 过渡：连接两端的「桥」。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Name a transitional fossil.<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Tiktaalik (fish to tetrapod) or Archaeopteryx (dinosaur to bird).<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.homologous-structure", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">ho<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">MOL<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">o<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">gous<\/span> <span class=\"st\">STRUC<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ture<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"homologous structure\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: homologous structure\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"homologous structure\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"28\" width=\"90\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"51\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Human arm<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">same bones: upper<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">arm, forearm, hand<\/text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"28\" width=\"90\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"149\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Bat wing<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">same bones, used<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">for flying<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A body part that is alike in different species because they share a common ancestor.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>同源结构<\/b>：不同物种中因有共同祖先而相似的身体部分。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">homo = same, logos = relation. Same origin.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">homo = 相同；同一来源。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: A human arm and a bat wing have the same bones. What kind of structure is this?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Homologous.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.analogous-structure", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">a<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">NAL<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">o<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">gous<\/span> <span class=\"st\">STRUC<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ture<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"analogous structure\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: analogous structure\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"analogous structure\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"28\" width=\"90\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"51\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Bird wing<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">bones + feathers<\/text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"28\" width=\"90\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"149\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Insect wing<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">thin membrane, no<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">bones<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A body part with a similar job in different species that did not come from a common ancestor part.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>同功结构<\/b>：不同物种中功能相似、但并非来自共同祖先同一结构的身体部分。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">ana- = according to. Analogy = similar job.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">analogy = 功能相似的类比。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Do a bird wing and an insect wing show homology or analogy?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Analogy. They fly, but do not share a common ancestor structure.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.vestigial-structure", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">ves<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">TIG<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">i<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">al<\/span> <span class=\"st\">STRUC<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ture<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"vestigial structure\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: vestigial structure\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"vestigial structure\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"55\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"22\" class=\"f1\"/><path d=\"M160 55 L185 45 L185 65 Z\" class=\"f1\"/><circle cx=\"55\" cy=\"52\" r=\"2\" class=\"\"/><ellipse cx=\"105\" cy=\"78\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"4\" class=\"f7\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">tiny hip bones<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"15\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">whale<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A reduced body part that has little or no use now but had a use in ancestors.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>退化结构<\/b>：如今作用很小或没有作用、但祖先中有功能的退化器官。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">vestigium = footprint, a trace left behind.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">vestigium = 足迹：留下的痕迹。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Whales have tiny hip bones. What do we call them?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Vestigial structures.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.comparative-embryology", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">com<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">PAR<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">a<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tive<\/span> <span class=\"sy\">em<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">bry<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">OL<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">o<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">gy<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"comparative embryology\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: comparative embryology\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"comparative embryology\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"35\" cy=\"55\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"18\" class=\"f2\"/><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"55\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"18\" class=\"f2\"/><ellipse cx=\"165\" cy=\"55\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"18\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"35\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">fish<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">chicken<\/text><text x=\"165\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">human<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">early embryos look alike<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">Comparing the early development of different species, which looks very alike in related groups.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>比较胚胎学<\/b>：比较不同物种的早期胚胎发育；亲缘相近的类群胚胎很相似。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">embryo = the earliest stage of development.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">embryo = 最早期的发育阶段。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What does embryology show about vertebrates?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Their early embryos look very similar, which points to a common ancestor.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.molecular-evidence", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">mo<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">LEC<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">u<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">lar<\/span> <span class=\"st\">EV<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">i<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">dence<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"molecular evidence\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: molecular evidence\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"molecular evidence\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">DNA similarity to humans<\/text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"36\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">chimp<\/text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"62\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">mouse<\/text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"88\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">yeast<\/text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"40\" width=\"90\" height=\"12\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f1\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"66\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f2\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"92\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f3\"/><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">Similarities in DNA or proteins between species, showing how closely related they are.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>分子证据<\/b>：不同物种 DNA 或蛋白质的相似程度，反映亲缘关系远近。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">molecule = a tiny unit of matter; DNA is a molecule that keeps the record.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">DNA 是记录亲缘的分子。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Which species shares more DNA with humans: a chimpanzee or a mouse?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">The chimpanzee.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.antibiotic-resistance", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">an<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ti<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">bi<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">OT<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">ic<\/span> <span class=\"sy\">re<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">SIS<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tance<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"antibiotic resistance\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: antibiotic resistance\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"antibiotic resistance\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"53.6\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Antibiotic<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"62.8\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">kills most<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">bacteria<\/text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"73.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"73.0,60.0 68.5,62.2 68.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"52.95\" font-size=\"9.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Resistant<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"63.15\" font-size=\"9.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">ones<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"73.35\" font-size=\"9.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">survive<\/text><line x1=\"127.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"141.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"141.0,60.0 136.5,62.2 136.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"52.95\" font-size=\"9.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Resistant<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"63.15\" font-size=\"9.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">bacteria<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"73.35\" font-size=\"9.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">multiply<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">The ability of bacteria to survive an antibiotic, which spreads by natural selection.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>抗生素耐药性<\/b>：细菌抵抗抗生素而存活的能力，会通过自然选择扩散。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">anti = against, bio = life. Resistance = a refusal to be killed.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">anti = 对抗；bio = 生命；resistance = 抵抗。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Why does using antibiotics too often cause resistance?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">It kills the non-resistant bacteria, so the resistant ones survive and multiply.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u2.t.sexual-selection", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term sm\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">SEX<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">u<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">al<\/span> <span class=\"sy\">se<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">LEC<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tion<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"sexual selection\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: sexual selection\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"sexual selection\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"22\" width=\"90\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"51\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Peacock&#x27;s tail<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">attracts a mate,<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">but makes escape<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">harder<\/text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"22\" width=\"90\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"149\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Result<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">males with showier<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">tails get more<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">mates<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">Selection for traits that help an organism win a mate, such as a peacock&#x27;s tail.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>性选择<\/b>：对有助于获得配偶的性状的选择，如孔雀的尾羽。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">sex = about mates.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">sexual = 与配偶有关。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What does sexual selection favour?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Traits that help an individual get mates.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}], "quiz": [{"id": "cu.q.u2.t.fossil", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“The preserved remains or traces of an organism that lived long ago.”<\/i>", "opts": ["fossil", "homologous structure", "fitness", "vestigial structure"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>fossil<\/b>: The preserved remains or traces of an organism that lived long ago. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">化石<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u2.t.transitional-fossil", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A fossil that shows traits of both an older group and the group that came after it.”<\/i>", "opts": ["fitness", "transitional fossil", "evolution", "genetic drift"], "a": 1, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>transitional fossil<\/b>: A fossil that shows traits of both an older group and the group that came after it. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">过渡化石<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u2.t.homologous-structure", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A body part that is alike in different species because they share a common ancestor.”<\/i>", "opts": ["homologous structure", "sexual selection", "geographic isolation", "artificial selection"], "a": 0, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>homologous structure<\/b>: A body part that is alike in different species because they share a common 